==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Zroco]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
**3 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn, delay 43.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Red EnerG]]s spawn, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Forcefully burrow the Zrocos and Zory with [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], then stall them with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]. Use that time to build up your wallet, then send out [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] once they push too close. [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] the second Zory so that he doesn't isolate your attackers by burrowing, as that can prematurely summon the boss wave. Once your units deal with the opening peons and start making their way to the enemy base, send out Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to hit the base and instantly chunk the first Red EnerG twice. From this point on, use Long Distance attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]] to gradually wear him down, using the peons as stepping stones. [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] helps immensely in this process.

Getting even one of the Red EnerGs off the field alleviates much of the frontline pressure, so it's only a matter of time until the second bites the dust. Try not to kill Lord Gravey prematurely, as he's your primary stepping stone.

==='''4 Crown Strategy'''===
The above strategy becomes exponentially easier with units such as [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Paperboy Cat]] joining the fray. In fact, it's quite possible to lock the enemies in place at the enemy base and subsequently beat them to a bloody pulp. Just use [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] to thin out the Zombies at the beginning instead of Housewife Cat.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
As is typically the case with [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] levels of this difficulty, an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] like [[Mighty Thermae D-Lux (Uber Rare Cat)|Subterra Sentinels]] will work very well for cleaning up after the Red EnerGs are gone. Alternatively, [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] and [[Queen Reika (Uber Rare Cat)|Reika]] are solid choices, thanks to their good [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] compatibility.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Chronos]]: Has a high standing range, which allows her to avoid getting hit by Red EnerG's [[Surge Attack|Surges]], while also freezing him and giving other units a chance to damage him. Her DPS is also acceptable and may help with clearing peons, though using her as the main source of damage would be unwise.
*[[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-02]]: Also has a high standing range and can use the peons as a stepping stone without getting hit often. If hit multiple times, its Strengthen ability will activate, allowing it to make quick work of the [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] rascals.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: While not particularly good against the Red Ener-G's or Lord Gravy, Balrog serves to deal with the Scissoroo, who would otherwise cause issues with pushing into your Housewifes and Li'l King Dragons. If they get a hit on Lord Gravey, they can absolutely melt them.
*[[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Thundia β]]: While not Surge Immune, Thundia comfortably outranges Lord Gravey. While Red EnerG's Surge Attacks may snipe her, she stands just at the edge of their effective range, letting her avoid the attack more often than not. Even one hit will shred the Red EnerG's, and she's more than likely going to land a few.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Targets everything in this stage. Though not Surge Immune, thus putting her at risk of getting juggled by Red EnerG, her Freeze and good damage makes the stage a lot more manageable by preventing the enemies from pushing.
*[[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|B.C.S. Beartooth]]: With a faster attack rate than its previous form, B.C.S. Beartooth's [[Dodge|Dodge Talent]], dual-effectiveness, and high range against both Red and Zombie enemies makes it a great, tanky pick to dispose of both [[Red EnerG]] and [[Lord Gravey]]; just be sure to defend it from [[Scissoroo]] provided that the latter is still present.

==Trivia==
*Border Soil may be a mistranslation. Its Japanese name, Tonariau Meido (隣り合う冥土), more closely translates to "Adjacent Netherworld" or "Adjacent World of the Dead" (hence the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]), but the kanji 土 in 冥土 (netherworld/world of the dead) means "soil", "mud" or "earth", which may explain the English name.

